Third-party components and external services
====================================================================

1. Adobe Photoshop / UXP
   This plugin runs inside the Adobe Photoshop UXP host and uses Adobe's public APIs.
   It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or certified by Adobe. "Adobe" and "Photoshop"
   are trademarks of Adobe, used only to describe the runtime environment.

2. ComfyUI (https://github.com/comfyanonymous/ComfyUI)
   The plugin only calls ComfyUI's public HTTP endpoints (/prompt, /history, /upload/image,
   ...). It does not include, link against, or modify ComfyUI source, so it is not a
   derivative work. Your own ComfyUI installation and custom nodes are governed by their
   own licenses (ComfyUI is GPL-3.0).

3. Image generation services
   The plugin calls third-party inference services over HTTPS. Their terms of service,
   content policies, billing and data handling are set by each provider. API keys are stored
   only on your machine and are never uploaded to any server of this project (the project
   has no server).

4. Model names
   gpt-image, nano-banana, FLUX, Klein, SDXL and similar names are trademarks or product
   names of their respective owners. They are used here only to select a model, and imply
   no affiliation, agency or endorsement.

5. Icons and fonts
   Icons under icons/ are made for this project. The UI uses system fonts only
   (SF Pro / PingFang SC on macOS, Segoe UI / Microsoft YaHei on Windows); no font files
   are distributed with this project.

